A||N||27||b lo 0||Who have you whipped??||||2||
Z||000000||b lo 0||07-24-2000||12:27 PM||||I'd like to start a thread-Anyone and everyone post your experiences showing up other cars-blasting by that RX-7 at 100 mph, killing that tricked Acura Integra from a stoplight, etc.  OK, OK, I'll start.  Some buds of mine and I got together to verify some bragging rights.  Well, I was up against Matt in his '93 Gran Prix.  He wasn't that surprised that I beat him, he knows I've got better power-weight ratios.  The next run was the best.  I was up against Nick in his '94 Bronco.  He thinks he's the baddest and fastest on the road-especially with his '90 Mustang Cobra 5.0 motor in there.  Well, due to his enourmous stereo (about 150 lbs) and large amount of unsprung weight (read: bad launch) I proceeded to kill him from the word go.  His jaw dropped as he got out of the truck, and began making excuses.   "I told you I need to get the Positrac replaced..."  The last race, the '79 Mustang Cobra, I didn't fare so well in.  But that's a different thread...<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||2
Z||000001||Formula||07-24-2000||02:51 PM||||I beat a 2000 mustang V6 5 speed from a stoplight to 60..... thats about it, oh yeah and  Ibeat a celica automatic, but with 100 ft lbs of tq how could it beat me?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Robert||07-24-2000||02:53 PM||||So I’m at a single, waiting for the green light so I can cross 4 lanes and get to the onramp.  This Mustang snuggles up behind me, the light turns green and I do a normal take off.  He is right on my bumper.  This onramp has two lanes with a hard 180 turn, (sign says slow to 30mph….and means it….)  We enter the ramp a about 25 and I decide I’ve had enough of this guy on my bumper.  I hit the gas and come out of the turn just below 60mph.  I look in my mirror and there is no Mustang to be seen…. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Shortly he blows by me doing 90 on the straight.   Didn’t even look at me……<P>Robert<BR><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> ||||reg||10
Z||000003||86SE||07-24-2000||03:20 PM||||I raced a full sized chevy pickup with a full load of steal and wood.  Neck and neck to 100MPH..........the guy laughed at me<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Fiero||||reg||10
Z||000004||88formula||07-24-2000||10:30 PM||||I have not won any races against any real sports cars yet. I have raced a late model Honda Prelude and it beat me by a door. I raced a Porsche 944 and that thing killed me. I raced a Honda CRX and although I beat him off the line he blew by me also. I did take a late model f body though in the corner. He was stuck to my bumper like I was towing him until we entered one of those 180-degree on ramps onto the highway. I went through there at about 55mph and when I came out I had about 100 feet on him, he then past me at about 90 mph. That was fun!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||07-24-2000||10:44 PM||||When I had the 85se (4cyl) I used to race the mailman almost everyday in his jeep. After adding the MSD and coil, gutted cat, dual exhaust muffler and a LiteSpeed sticker I could kinda pull away from him until I hit third.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Megafiero||07-24-2000||11:01 PM||||I'v raced some newer BMW 4 door,  don't remember what the numbers where,  I had him till 130, then he had the advantage of a 5 speed over my 4 speed.<P>Megafiero<BR>85" GT 2.9L||||reg||1
Z||000007||Klown||07-24-2000||11:50 PM||||I once had a guy in a riced up toyota paseo rev his engine at me at a stop light.  I was going to led it slide but my buddy really wanted to me to race him.  It was one of those funky "right turn on arrow only" intersections so I didn't realize the light was going to turn green when it did.  So the paseo takes off ahead of me while I still have to shift into first and make a less than smooth start.  I caught up to him once I was in second and just left him behind once I was in third.  I saw that the light ahead of me was going to turn red so I slowed so that I could have a go at it again.  This ricer must not have wanted to play anymore because he blew right thru that red.  Not bad for the little V6 considering my buddy weighs over 300 lbs!||||reg||6
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||07-25-2000||12:00 AM||||At the track doing the autocross thing I have whipped many vehicles that should have kicked my booty.<P>The ones I am most proud of are:<P>2 91 MR2's, 91 Eagle Talon TSi, 87 MR2,00 Integra Type R and a few others  <A HREF="http://www.team.net/urscca/results/2000/000416.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.team.net/urscca/results/2000/000416.html</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe||||reg||1
Z||000009||b lo 0||07-25-2000||09:38 AM||||This one just happened last night.  I was at a stop sign on Temple Johnson Road (one of the twistiest roads in Gwinnett County) and pulling off, driving regularly.  I noticed a Buick Grand National pulled out behind me, complete with big-n-littles and gauges on the hood.  I knew this guy would whoop my ass with the turbo V6 in those things in a straight line, so I chilled out.  He seemed pretty relaxed too.  Anyways, we finished passing these kids walking on the side of the road, so I gave it all I had. He mighta had me beat in the accelleration department, but Ice whipped through those corners like nothin else.  He tried his darnedest, and, granted, whenever we hit a straight he (I'm guessing) hit his nitrous and rode my ass, but in the corners I had him beat.  As he turned off the road, I flashed my brake lights at him, thanking him for a good time.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>GAWD I love this car||||reg||10
Z||000010||loafer87gt||07-25-2000||12:28 PM||||I lent my car to my Mom and Dad for a weekend a couple of summers ago and some guy in a early 70's Porshe 911 tried to race him. I guess Dad tromped it and left the guy in his porsche in his dust! Mom said she hadn't seen Dad grin like that for a long time! My personal kills are a non-turbo 91 Stealth, 2.2 and 2.4 litre turbo Daytonas (surprisingly quick cars), 92 Civic SI (riced up with intake and exhaust), and my favorite, a 84 Vette. The vette was the coolest race ever, we both took off from the lights and we were both waiting for the other guy to make the first move. I heard him kinda goose it a bit so I hammered it down in first and took it up to the redline before slamming it into second, making a nice loud sqawk before hooking up. The coolest thing about the race (which lasted about 5 blocks) is that whenever I shifted into 3rd or downshifted into second I chirped my tires. At the end of the race we had to stop for a intersection at the bottom of the hill and in order to slow down I had to downshift into second at 85 KPH which caused the back end to lock up briefly leaving another nice patch. At the intersection the guy in the vette wouldn't make eye contact. Another kill for the plastic fantastic. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Haze_Performance||07-25-2000||12:39 PM||||Well I smoked a new riced up civic last week. Not the coolest looking race in the world, but he sure felt the sh!t.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Haze_sig_1.gif">  My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A> &                  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>H.M.P. </A>||||reg||6
Z||000012||GT Bastard||07-25-2000||01:10 PM||||Recently whipped the same late-model eclipse GS(non-turbo) on my way home from work two nights in a row.  Hardly proud of that one... I wouldn't of raced him at all, but he had dealer plates and 3 girls with him.  I thought it would be funny to make an example of him.  Then there was an early model Firebird T/A(junked-out) that tried to pick a race.  He was a joke too.||||reg||1
Z||000013||1FST2M6||07-25-2000||01:42 PM||||YEAH! Give em hell jeff! (GT Bastard)   ||||reg||1
Z||000014||rogergarrison||07-25-2000||06:34 PM||||my latest encounters included a late model C-5 Corvette, 2000 MonteCarlo SS, both wide open on interstates. I won. Oh yea, and a couple months ago me and a new Porsche Boxter run bumper to bumper for about 40 miles on a country 2 lane. BTW i have an 86 se with a Ferrari kit body, its powere is Z-24 3.1, with Turbo||||reg||1
Z||000015||Old Lar||07-25-2000||08:27 PM||||The last car I beat in a streetdrag was a Fiero SE.  It was one of the few time I got second gear rubber with my GT when I shifted.  Homey don't do that any more.<P>Now I just use cruise and love it when some one starts tailgating.  I click on the cruise and slowly increase the speed.  I had some clown in a Chrysler product on my bumper until he realized he was doing over 100 and quickly dropped back.||||reg||10
Z||000016||RobertVol||07-25-2000||09:07 PM||||I usually dont take my 3.8 SC out but on the weekends. My car "LOOKS" stock. I had a guy try to race me with his stock 5.0 stang. He sat there at the light and laughed and reved it on and on. I acted like I ignored him UNTIL the light turned green. Then it was see ya ! and I had the tops out and could here him get on it try to catch up. but to no avail I was gone ! I pulled in at the next gas station I came to but were he could see me pull in. He "finally" caught up and pulled in all he could say was Man I better make sure I check before I run my car~ all I could say was ....Uhhhhhh  YEAH !  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/3eab6a20.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000017||filthyscarecrow||07-26-2000||02:01 AM||||yeah, i embarrassed a few poeple too. i got to drive some touring laps at road america in elkhart lake wisconsin with my 86 se. it used to be my dad's car, but he passed away a few months ago. i blew by a BMW 580i going up the front straight hill (big hill too, little car shouldn't be able to do that, right?). some wad in a vette kept holding me up until i got about a 20 mph run on him coming out of the carousel (his tires were squealing, mine weren't) and kissed him goodbye. i also disposed of a porsche 944 coming out of turn 5 and going up the hill. i'll have pics pretty soon if anyone is interested.<BR>i'm sure dad was giggling like a little kid watching what his car could do. i know i was...<P>------------------<BR>me go fast.||||reg||4
Z||000018||Standard||07-26-2000||04:34 AM||||Another minnesota member! And a bike mechanic to boot!  You rule man!  I've wrenched on bikes for 4 years now.  Where do you work, if you don't mind me asking?  I worked at Bennett's cycle for those 4 years until they closed up about 3 weeks ago.. <P>How far away is that course from the cities?  I'd like to get out there sometime and see what the ole' GT can do..<P>------------------<BR>Mike -- Golden Valley, MN<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 147,000 miles and counting!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||GT Bastard||07-26-2000||05:23 AM||||Almost forgot... Two '86 SE's.  The first one was another gold SE with a Isuzu transplant.  We raced on a back country road from 0-60.  I really screwed up my launch and bogged down badly from the start, but as soon as it caught up I was able to pull on him steadily.  The other was against a red '86 SE 4-sp with a 3.1 transplant.  I've seen his car take a 5.0 through a light so I thought it would be interesting.  We are crossing an overpass after pulling away from a stoplight on 4-lane at night and he provoked me(friend of mine.)  We both nailed it at around 30mph and raced to 80 or so.  REALLY close.  I had him pretty good from the start, and then we evened up.  I could just barely pull away from him.  <P>I'm really curious to see what the 3.2 is going to do to this car with it's current mods. In case anyone is wondering, the mods were completed by 1FST2M6...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold 86 SE V6 4-sp w/4.10 gears, Eibach springs, Koni's all around w/some poly bushings<BR>Yoko's<BR>Coated headers<BR>ACT 4-puck clutch<BR>MSD ignition<BR>Flowmaster w/ mandrel bent 2.5 pipe<BR>extrude honed intake<BR>Lots of fuel system mods... etc etc...||||reg||1
Z||000020||vinnywolfe||07-26-2000||11:48 AM||||first kill!<BR>last night i picked up my 87 gt that i have been working on from the body shop where i had a 4 wheel alignment done, car drives EXCELLENT now, anyway at a light these two teenagers in a le Baron gt or gtc (something like that) pull up and kinda start snickering at me.  keep in mind that my car is primer color.  i'm still looking for someone to paint it.  and although i have the new sail panels, i wanted to wait till it was painted to put them on.  <BR>well, when the light turned green, i could tell he wanted to impress his friend.  not EVEN a contest.  i WASTED him from the get-go.  probably nothing to be proud of, but it's my FIRST kill with my gt and i hope to have many more.<P>later,<BR>vinny<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000021||lou_dias||07-26-2000||01:31 PM||||My kills include a 2000 Mustang GT on the highway he took off on me from just under 80mph so I then punched it, kept gaining and then really pulled after 115mph;<P>an 81 suped up Olds Cutlass with dual exhaust.  He was close, I creaped by him and only pulled 2 car lenghts ahead after half a mile.  It started at 75mph to about 120mph.<BR>I'm sure I would have beat him 0-60 easily, especially off the line.<P>I don't look for races, I cruise at 75 and just pass people because I am doing 75 then they decide to get on my ass and pass me and depending on how they do it, then I'll punch it or not.<P>My car is a Fiero Factory 3.4(rebuilt) with ported heads and intake, hollow cat, IRM dual exhaust, K&N filter, Spiralmax, Bosch 4 way plugs, Accel coil, 1.52 roller rockers, Crane Compucam.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||Oreif||07-26-2000||01:41 PM||||Spiralmax!?! Honestly did you really see a difference between with and without the spiralmax? You should try the "piston springs" too. I hear they work as well as the spiralmax.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.getodd.com/more/springs/springs.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.getodd.com/more/springs/springs.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 07-26-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000023||lou_dias||07-27-2000||12:27 PM||||You got to be pooping me about the piston rings.  Seriously...<P>All I got to say about Spiralmax is that with my ported heads, intake, etc... I lost some bottom end.  SpiralMax gave me some of that back and better fuel economy.<P>SpiralMax is really popular with rice rockets.  There is also another device that performs a similar function for foreign cars and it's bigger and cone shaped...<P>Current head designs are designed to swirl the air coming into the combusiton chamber to improve the air/fuel mixture.  SpiralMax adds lots of turbulence to the air as it enters your intake.  Read: TURBULENCE IS GOOD.<P>Sure it costs $1 to make, but I don't have a CNC machine in my back yard...||||reg||1
Z||000024||FIEROCIOUS||07-27-2000||10:52 PM||||My 87 GT kills (before new engine)<P>95' Eagle Talon turbo 4wd<BR>94' Mustang GT 4.8<BR>95' Mustang with hella mods sounded "BAD ACE"<BR>he actualy was faster but the Fiero takes off from a standing start way better.<BR>From light to light Fiero allways wins!<BR>Zillions of Civics and Civic SI's<BR>99' Mitsu Eclipse<BR>85' bridge port RX7 spec 7<BR>72' Chevy Camaro 402<BR>An Integra or two<P>I beat a Viper in my 73' Nova. but that's a differant story. <P>I'll have to see what the new engine will do!||||reg||1
Z||000025||Shaun41178||07-28-2000||10:44 PM||||i have had numerous kills with my fiero.  I have posted many of them here at the forum.  However I did get into a race last week with a 89 Mustang Lx 5.0 automatic.  We talked before we raced.  He had plenty of mods too.  He said it had Intake, 1.7 rockers, pulleys, shorty headers, cat-back with "h" pipe and flowmasters and 3.73 gears.  I did get to see the intake mod as it went into the fender opening so I had to take his word on the other mods.  I don't know why he would lie though.  SO anyway we lined up ona deserted road and had a guy flag us.  I left his ass right from the beginning.  i had a good one car leas within the first 60 feet of the race.  I took him all the way through the qtr mile as we mark it off on this street.  It was funny.  His girl was at the finish line and from what I am told he was pretty embarrased.  My boss was with me and he said he sounded pretty upset.  I love whooping up on stangs.  Funny thing was this guy claimes 14.0 flat on a g-tech.  HAHAHA.  <P>A less fun race came by a Toyota supra turbo of like a 87 model year or so.  Guy wanted to race for money but I declined.  We raced, I beat him bad, and then asked if he wanted to race again for money.  he of course didnt want to.  <P>My mods include Nitrous, pulley, and my own intake design as well as a few others that don't really make much of a difference.  You can read about them on my webpage.  I hope to update that sometime soon too.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Shaun-Toledo OH, 85 GT<BR>3.2 With nitrous<BR>http://members.aol.com/shaun41178||||reg||1
Z||000026||fieroshop||07-29-2000||12:00 AM||||I raced several cars and beat most of them, then one night I had a an Eclipse with lot of modifications and he wanted to race. We were both going on the freeway and the unramp narrowed down to one lane. I took him from the start and he tried to keep up with me thru the S curve and what he did was slide sideways and hit the rail. Needless to say I don,t do much racing anymore unless I go to a race track. I forgot to say I was a race driver in Europe when I was younger and in my 20's||||reg||1
Z||000027||GT Bastard||07-29-2000||12:03 AM||||Shaun, you've gotta get us some pics of the aluminum block.  ||||reg||1
